    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36974" root="كسر" body-key="k">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِسْرَوِىٌّ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِسْرِىٌّ</span></b>  <i>Of,</i> or <i>relating to,</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِسْرَى</span>; rel. ns. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِسْرَى</span>: (S, Msb, K:)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَسْرَوِىٌّ</span> alone is the rel. n. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَسْرَى</span>.
(Msb.) [In the TA, it is said that one should
not say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَسْرَوِىٌّ</span>; but it seems that what is not
allowable is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَسْرِىٌّ</span>.]

